{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b3hyv2622","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Howp5g2Bgii4PWohKWiH6g","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/6fb62287-6dc4-404d-8820-92006ff4cb2a/tasks/b3hyv2622.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_0/candidate_1\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople keep a running tally of heads versus tails as they read a sequence and track which side is \"in the lead\"; a fair coin, they expect, lets the lead change hands, so a sequence in which one side stays ahead for a long unbroken stretch of the path (HHTHTHTH: heads leads at every flip although no streak is longer than two and the counts are nearly even) looks biased and so less random, by a shared weight on the longest stretch of flips during which the tally never returns to balance. This sits on top of the current best judgement (each person's own ideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, and a personal guessing rate), so it is the path's lead persistence, not how far the tally strays, that is added.\nEOF\necho lead_persistence_aversion > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"models/most_lopsided_stretch_aversion.py\").read()\ndoc_end = src.index('\"\"\"', 3) + 3\nsrc = '''\"\"\"Lead persistence: a running tally whose lead never changes hands looks biased.\n\nPeople keep a running tally of heads versus tails while reading and track which\nside is ahead; a sequence in which one side stays ahead for a long unbroken\nstretch (the tally never returning to balance) looks biased and less random, by\na shared weight on the longest such stretch. This sits on the current best\njudgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on\nimbalance and the longest run, shared weights on the final run, mirror\nsymmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, personal lapse).\n\"\"\"''' + src[doc_end:]\nsrc = src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''', '''    def lead_persistence(seq):\n        # Longest stretch of consecutive flips after which the same side leads\n        # (tally never back at balance), as a share of the sequence.\n        tally, best, cur, sign = 0, 0, 0, 0\n        for x in seq:\n            tally += 1 if x == \"H\" else -1\n            s = (tally > 0) - (tally < 0)\n            if s != 0 and s == sign:\n                cur += 1\n            elif s != 0:\n                cur = 1\n            else:\n                cur = 0\n            sign = s\n            best = max(best, cur)\n        return max(best - 1, 0) / (len(seq) - 1)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc = src.replace('''        \"lopsided_b\": lopsided_stretch(b),\n''', '''        \"lopsided_b\": lopsided_stretch(b),\n        \"lead_a\": lead_persistence(a),\n        \"lead_b\": lead_persistence(b),\n''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(''', '''    lead_a = pm.Data(\"lead_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    lead_b = pm.Data(\"lead_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    # Personal lapse''', '''    # Shared penalty on lead persistence (positive: a lead that never changes hands looks biased).\n    xi = pm.Normal(\"xi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n\n    # Personal lapse''')\nsrc = src.replace(\"- eta * lopsided_a\\n\", \"- eta * lopsided_a - xi * lead_a\\n\")\nsrc = src.replace(\"- eta * lopsided_b\\n\", \"- eta * lopsided_b - xi * lead_b\\n\")\nassert src.count(\"xi * lead_\") == 2\nopen(\"iter_0/candidate_1/candidate.py\", \"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_1')\n\" ; /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_1 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"52a17180-dff6-48a0-bb5b-8c13341b0b9b","session_id":"6fb62287-6dc4-404d-8820-92006ff4cb2a"}
