{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcwGarRaiXHYK2f5kg4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate is written and the self-check passed: it prints `OK` and gives a finite ELPD-LOO of −3537.6 on the short smoke fit. Two caveats from that fit: 8.5% of trials had high Pareto-k, so its PSIS-LOO estimate was flagged as unreliable, and convergence wasn't checked because a single chain can't report R-hat. Admission's full multi-chain fit will settle both, and it may reject the model. Novelty against the other models wasn't checked either.\n\n**Model:** `lead_persistence_aversion`\n\n**Hypothesis:** As people read a sequence they keep a running count of heads versus tails and notice which side is ahead. They expect a fair coin to let the lead change hands, so a sequence where one side stays ahead for a long unbroken stretch looks biased. HHTHTHTH is the clearest case: heads leads at every flip, even though no streak is longer than two and the counts are nearly even.\n\n**How it's built:**\n- The new feature is the longest stretch of flips during which the same side stays ahead without the tally returning to balance, as a share of the sequence length.\n- It enters as one shared weight added to the current best model's judgement, `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion`. Everything else in that model is unchanged.\n- It is different from the two earlier tally-based models that were dropped:\n  - `tally_drift_ideal` and `running_lead_surprise_path` measured how far the tally drifted or how surprising the lead was. This one measures how long a lead lasts.\n  - The current best model already uses how far the tally strays (its \"most lopsided stretch\"). Lead persistence separates sequences that one doesn't: HHTHTHTH and HTTHHTTH score the same on lopsidedness (0.14) but 1.0 versus 0.0 on lead persistence.\n\nIt doesn't address the critique's side-bias findings, and those didn't survive the false-discovery correction anyway (q = 0.14 and 0.18).\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2687,"cache_read_input_tokens":77438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2687,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fb62287-6dc4-404d-8820-92006ff4cb2a","uuid":"1e15e158-58b7-4bcd-907b-6da38cf033ac","timestamp":"2026-10-02T06:28:02.157Z","request_id":"req_011CfcwGaS8DejwBo4CcXeZS"}
